WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.200
You know the feeling you get
when you learn something new

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:06.600
about a health problem
you’ve been trying to reverse?

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:10.080
Maybe high blood pressure,
diabetes, or heart disease.

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:13.740
Well, there’s nothing I like better
than bringing you the information

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:16.500
that will help you do just that.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:19.080
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast.

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:21.900
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:25.320
Today we explore
what dietary change

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:30.364
can simultaneously help detoxify mercury,
lead, and cadmium from the body.

00:00:30.691 --> 00:00:31.980
We’ve previously explored

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:33.840
the issue of lead contamination in

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:36.000
calcium supplements like bone meal,

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.560
but it wasn’t just bone meal.

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:39.180
Substantial quantities of lead

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:40.440
were found in other, more common,

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:41.880
over-the-counter supplements.

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:43.980
Still, testing revealed continued

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:45.840
public health concern over bone meal,

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:48.180
but thankfully it’s not
as popular these days.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:49.920
So, many of us are not likely

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:51.900
to get directly exposed to the lead

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:53.400
in bone meal any more –

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:56.400
but may get indirectly exposed

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:57.720
through the animals we eat.

00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:00.900
In the U.S., five billion pounds

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:02.820
of meat and bone meal are produced

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:04.680
as slaughterhouse by-products every year.

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:07.560
What do we do with these millions

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:08.640
of tons every year?

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:11.460
We feed it back to farm animals,

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:12.600
particularly chickens.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:14.760
Now, most of the lead in the bone meal

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:15.960
passes right through the animals

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:18.120
into their waste, but then we take

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:20.160
that waste (cow, pig, and chicken feces)

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:23.100
and feed it back to the animals again.

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:23.880
You guessed it!

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:25.380
So, you can see how the levels

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:27.660
of contaminants might
buildup in their body.

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:30.780
I’ve talked previously about
what that might mean for

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:32.100
making something like chicken soup,

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:33.900
but the original concern about

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:35.280
these kinds of feeding practices,

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:38.580
of feeding cows to cows,
and pigs and chickens,

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:40.500
was the spread of prion diseases,

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:41.880
like mad cow disease,

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:44.700
but it’s not just prions that

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:47.160
this kind of recycling can magnify;

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:49.620
but other toxic substances including lead.

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:51.960
So, a more plant-based diet

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:54.060
may be able to lower lead exposure,

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:56.460
and an even more plant-based diet

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:58.620
could theoretically lower
exposure even more,

00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:02.220
but you’ve got to put it to the test.

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:05.640
But, should we expect to find a benefit?

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:08.160
Yes, lead is one of the
toxins found in meat,

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:11.340
but half of our dietary exposure

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:13.620
probably comes from plant foods.

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:15.960
Dietary modeling studies in Europe

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:17.640
suggest that vegetarians would be

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:19.380
exposed to about the same amount

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:21.420
of lead compared to
the general population,

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:23.220
with the exception of those

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:24.840
who eat a lot of wild game,

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:26.580
which can end up with a thousand times

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:28.080
more lead than most other foods.

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:32.460
In fact, a vegetarian diet
may even be higher in lead.

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:34.620
But, it’s not what you eat;

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:36.600
it’s what you absorb.

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:39.600
As we learned from the cadmium story,

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:41.880
the uptake of toxic heavy metals

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:44.220
from animal food sources into the human

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:46.920
intestinal lining cells may be higher

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:48.660
than that from vegetable sources.

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:51.600
That’s how you have a vegetarian

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:53.280
with some of the lowest concentrations

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:54.840
of lead and cadmium in her blood,

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:57.540
despite higher concentrations in her diet.

00:02:57.540 --> 00:03:01.080
But you don’t know, until you…

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:02.580
put it to the test.

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:05.640
There seemed to be a tendency towards

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:07.800
higher fecal elimination of lead

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:09.780
following a change to a vegetarian diet,

00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:12.000
with nine subjects on average tripling

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:13.140
their elimination of lead,

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:16.260
three unaffected, and four
dropping by about half.

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:18.900
But, the study only lasted a few months;

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:21.480
the difference wasn’t
statistically significant.

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:24.060
So, let’s try a year.

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:27.060
A shift towards a diet characterized

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:28.860
by large amounts of raw vegetables,

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:30.900
fruits, and unrefined foods, whole grains,

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:33.540
with the exclusion of
meat, poultry, fish, and eggs

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:36.000
(though it did include fermented dairy,

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:37.200
like a type of soured milk),

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:40.380
as well as cutting back on
processed foods and junk.

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:42.240
They took clippings of hair

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:43.560
before and after the shift,

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:47.700
and got significant reductions
in heavy metals,

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:49.320
including cutting their lead level

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:50.157
nearly in half.

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:51.840
And within three months,

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:53.340
their toxic heavy metals

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:56.700
went down, and stayed down.

00:03:57.600 --> 00:03:58.800
How do we know it wasn’t

00:03:58.800 --> 00:03:59.820
just a coincidence?

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:02.160
Because they went back up

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:02.820
a few years later

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:03.900
after the study was over,

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:04.980
after they went back to

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:06.000
more of their regular diet,

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:07.860
and their mercury, cadmium,

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:09.480
and lead levels shot back up

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:10.740
to where they were before.

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:13.500
Same thing with a different
group after two years.

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:16.080
The drop in mercury is easy to explain,

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:17.400
presumably due to the drastic drop

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:19.020
in fish consumption, and the drop

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:20.880
in alcoholic beverages may have

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:22.140
contributed to the drop in lead,

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:24.240
but it also could have been

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:25.620
a cadmium-like effect,

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:27.540
where the decrease in hair lead content

00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:29.100
could be due to the dietary shift

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:31.140
resulting in less absorption of lead

00:04:31.140 --> 00:04:33.794
into the body in the first place.

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:35.280
In our next story,

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:39.837
we look at one of the most concentrated
sources of the toxic metal cadmium.

00:04:40.140 --> 00:04:46.080
Cadmium is known as a highly toxic metal
that represents a major hazard to human health.

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:50.700
It sticks around in our body for decades because
our body has no efficient way to get rid of it,

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:56.580
and may contribute to a variety of illnesses,
including heart disease, cancer, and diabetes.

00:04:57.180 --> 00:05:00.780
Most recently, data suggests cadmium exposure

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:04.680
may impair cognitive performance even
at levels once thought to be safe.

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:09.060
Recent studies suggest&nbsp;
cadmium exposure may produce&nbsp;

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:11.280
adverse health effects at lower exposure levels

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:15.780
than previously predicted, including
increased risk of hormonal cancers.

00:05:15.780 --> 00:05:22.380
For example, researchers on Long Island
estimated that about 40% of breast cancer

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:26.460
in the U.S. might be associated
with elevated cadmium levels.

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:34.440
Inhalation of cigarette smoke is one of the
major routes for human exposure to cadmium.

00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:39.000
Seafood consumption is another dominant
route of human exposure in this study,

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:42.120
even more so than from cigarette smoke.

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:50.520
The highest levels, though, are found in organ
meats, but how many horse kidneys can you eat?

00:05:50.520 --> 00:05:55.080
Because people eat so few&nbsp;
organs, grains and vegetables&nbsp;

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:58.080
actually end up contributing the largest amount.

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:02.940
But wait a second, whole grains and vegetables
are among the major dietary sources

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:07.740
of fiber, phytoestrogens, antioxidants
that may protect against breast cancer.

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:13.800
And indeed, even though the risk of breast cancer
goes up as women consume more and more cadmium,

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:17.940
even though on paper, most cadmium
comes from grains and vegetables,

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:22.560
breast cancer risk goes down the more and
more whole grains and vegetables women eat,

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:27.180
so maybe the animal sourced&nbsp;
cadmium is somehow worse,

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:31.440
or the benefits of plant foods just overwhelm
any adverse effects of the cadmium?

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:35.640
This study may have helped solve the mystery.

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:39.900
It’s not what we eat. It’s what we absorb.

00:06:40.440 --> 00:06:46.500
Cadmium bioavailability from animal-based foods
may be higher than from vegetable-based foods.

00:06:46.500 --> 00:06:51.180
There appears to be something in plants
that inhibits cadmium absorption.

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:55.800
In fact, if you add kale&nbsp;
to your boiled pig kidneys,&nbsp;

00:06:55.800 --> 00:06:58.140
you can cut down on the toxic exposure.

00:06:58.140 --> 00:07:02.580
Just one tablespoon of pig kidney and
we may exceed the daily safety limit—

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:08.160
unless we eat kale, in which case
we could eat a whole quarter cup.

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:12.420
The pronounced effects of the inhibitory factors&nbsp;

00:07:12.420 --> 00:07:14.940
in kale point out the&nbsp;
importance of vegetable foods

00:07:14.940 --> 00:07:18.540
in terms of prevention of&nbsp;
health hazards from cadmium&nbsp;

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:21.660
ingested as mixed diets in a real situation.

00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:27.720
Even if a vegetarian diet contains more
lead and cadmium than a mixed diet,

00:07:27.720 --> 00:07:32.040
it is not certain that it will give
rise to higher uptake of the metals,

00:07:32.040 --> 00:07:34.920
because the absorption of lead and cadmium

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:38.820
is inhibited by plant compounds
such as fiber and phytate.

00:07:38.820 --> 00:07:41.100
And it’s not just in lab animals.

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:44.940
Having whole grains in our
stomach up to three hours

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:49.860
before we swallow lead can
eliminate 90% of absorption,

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:55.140
thought to be due to phytates in whole
grains, beans and nuts grabbing onto it.

00:07:56.100 --> 00:08:00.480
So vegetarians may have lower levels
even though they have higher intakes.

00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:05.880
In fact, a significant decrease in the hair
concentrations of lead and cadmium was seen

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:09.780
after the change from an omnivorous
to a vegetarian diet,

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:12.900
indicating a lower absorption of the metals.

00:08:12.900 --> 00:08:17.520
Here’s that study. They took folks
eating a standard Swedish diet

00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:20.460
and put them on a vegetarian diet.

00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:24.780
Lots of whole unrefined plant foods,
no meat, poultry, fish, eggs,

00:08:24.780 --> 00:08:28.413
and junk food was discouraged.
48&nbsp;

00:08:28.413 --> 00:08:29.820
00:03:58,9 --&gt; 00:04:01,166
Here’s where they started out: a measure

00:08:29.820 --> 00:08:35.466
of their mercury levels, cadmium levels,
and lead levels in their bodies.

00:08:35.466 --> 00:08:37.380
Within three months on a vegetarian diet,
their levels significantly dropped,

00:08:37.380 --> 00:08:41.160
and stayed down for the rest
of the year-long experiment.

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:43.860
But then they came back three years later,

00:08:43.860 --> 00:08:47.820
three years after they stopped eating
vegetarian. And what did they find?

00:08:47.820 --> 00:08:52.800
Their levels of mercury, cadmium
and lead shot back up.

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:57.180
Since the cadmium in plants is
based on the cadmium in soil,

00:08:57.180 --> 00:09:03.360
plant-eaters that live in a really
polluted area like Slovakia —

00:09:03.360 --> 00:09:10.260
which has some of the highest levels,
the so-called black triangle of pollution,

00:09:10.260 --> 00:09:14.520
thanks to the chemical and smelting industries —

00:09:14.520 --> 00:09:17.520
those who eat lots of plants
there can indeed build up

00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:21.300
higher cadmium levels, especially
if you eat lots of plants.

00:09:22.020 --> 00:09:26.280
It’s interesting, in spite of the significantly
higher blood cadmium concentration

00:09:26.280 --> 00:09:29.700
as a consequence of a greater
cadmium intake from polluted plants,

00:09:29.700 --> 00:09:35.100
all the antioxidants in those same plants were
found to help inhibit the harmful effects

00:09:35.100 --> 00:09:38.880
of higher free radical production
caused by the cadmium exposure.

00:09:39.840 --> 00:09:44.040
Still, though, in highly polluted areas
it might be an especially good idea

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:47.640
not to smoke, or eat too much
seafood or organ meats,

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:52.440
but even if we live in the Slovak Republic’s
black triangle of pollution,

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:57.360
the benefits of whole plant
foods would outweigh the risks.

00:09:57.360 --> 00:10:02.700
In highly polluted areas, zinc supplements
may decrease cadmium absorption,

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:06.780
but I’d recommend against
multi-mineral supplements,

00:10:06.780 --> 00:10:12.792
as they have been found to be
contaminated with cadmium itself.

00:10:13.680 --> 00:10:14.580
Finally today,

00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:19.320
did you know that the toxic heavy metal
contamination of Ayurvedic dietary supplements is,

00:10:19.320 --> 00:10:21.906
in most cases,
intentional?

00:10:22.320 --> 00:10:27.240
How do toxic heavy metals get into
Ayurvedic medicines in the first place?

00:10:28.380 --> 00:10:33.000
In most cases, high levels of metals in
Ayurvedic traditional herbal preparations

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:38.820
result from intentional incorporation
of certain metallic preparations

00:10:38.820 --> 00:10:44.760
like lead oxide, mercury sulfide,
arsenic trioxide.

00:10:45.600 --> 00:10:47.220
Not to worry, though.

00:10:47.220 --> 00:10:52.200
The heavy metals are claimed
to be detoxified by, for example,

00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:56.940
heating and cooling the
herbal mixtures in cow’s urine.

00:10:56.940 --> 00:10:59.700
This is not just an India issue.

00:10:59.700 --> 00:11:03.360
Traditional medicines from around
the world incorporate these poisons.

00:11:03.360 --> 00:11:08.940
In the Middle East, saoott is used
as a teething powder for infants.

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:11.100
It’s 51% lead;

00:11:11.820 --> 00:11:17.280
one of a number of black lead-containing
substances used as teething powder.

00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:22.680
Bokhoor is a Middle Eastern
practice of burning lead sulfides

00:11:22.680 --> 00:11:25.620
to produce pleasant
fumes to calm infants.

00:11:26.220 --> 00:11:27.600
They’ll be calm, all right.

00:11:27.600 --> 00:11:32.520
Traditional Latin American medicines
include azarcon and greta—

00:11:32.520 --> 00:11:36.900
almost pure lead,
used to treat constipation.

00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:43.200
In traditional Chinese herbal medicine,
mercury is considered to have a

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:48.060
tranquilizing and (if you can believe it)
detoxifying effect.

00:11:49.440 --> 00:11:50.400
But wait a second.

00:11:50.400 --> 00:11:52.440
Haven’t these remedies
been used for centuries?

00:11:52.440 --> 00:11:56.460
Sure, but that doesn’t
mean they’re safe.

00:11:57.120 --> 00:12:01.560
In the West, let’s not forget
that bloodletting was among

00:12:01.560 --> 00:12:05.700
the most common medical
practices performed by doctors

00:12:05.700 --> 00:12:09.062
for almost 2,000 years.

